<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Republic - Details of 1997 budget plan.</title>
<headline>Czech Republic - Details of 1997 budget plan.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows the proposed expenditure planned in the government's balanced 1997 state budget on which a final vote is expected on Friday.</p>
<p>The draft budget calls for equal revenue and expenditure of 549.1 billion crowns up from an originally approved 1996 balanced budget total of 497.6 billion crowns which was later revised to total 491 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The 1997 expenditure figures are compared with the figures originally approved for the 1996 budget.</p>
<p>The 1997 budget is based on growth in gross domestic product of 5.4 percent average annual inflation of 8.6 percent, a current account deficit of 5.8 percent and average unemployment of 3.3 percent: - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>						 FY 1997	   FY 1996</p>
<p>TOTAL EXPENDITURE    (CZK 000s)   549,099,964    497,641,000</p>
<p>Office of the President		   380,283	  307,169</p>
