<p>Note. The 1996 budget total was lowered to 491 billion crowns in the early autumn through across the board one percentage point spending cuts in each ministry's full-year budget in order to avoid a forecast 9.3 billion crown deficit, due to overspending and lower than expected revenues.</p>
<p>On Wednesday the cabinet froze December spending at selected ministries and required early repayment on credit from the state deposit insurance fund in order to keep the full-year 1996 accout within a deficit of 1.2 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
